<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Generic 2-Dimensional Oscillator (G2D) is a phenomenological, coupled, nonlinear two-dimensional (i.e., two state-variables ('V', 'W')) oscillatory, neural mass model. The G2D is a generalization of the well-known FitzHugh-Nagumo model (FitzHugh, 1961; Nagumo et. al, 1962), adapted here for reproducing a wilder class of dynamical configurations of physiological phenomena as observed in neuronal population using phase-portrait method." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/FitzHugh1961> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Nagumo1962> .
