# https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/DerivedVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Excitatory population firing rate. In full aLN this is ``Phi(mu_E_eff, s_EE)`` with ``Phi`` precomputed; here a sigmoid stand-in is used." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "r_E (CakanObermayer derived variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "r_E" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "r_E" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_E> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "r_max/(1 + exp(-k_phi*(mu_se - mu_th)))" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_I
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CakanObermayer/derived_variables/r_I> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
