# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/experiments/Schirner2023_MultiscaleBNM_DM
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/experiments/Schirner2023_MultiscaleBNM_DM> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/experiments/Schirner2023_MultiscaleBNM_DM> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SimulationExperiment> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/experiments/Schirner2023_MultiscaleBNM_DM> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Multiscale brain network model coupling large-scale structural connectivity with a small-scale frontoparietal circuit for decision-making (DM) and working memory (WM). The large-scale model uses the Reduced Wong-Wang model (Deco et al., 2014, JNeurosci) with explicit excitatory and inhibitory populations. The functional circuit implements winner-take-all DM and persistent-activity WM based on Murray, Jaramillo & Wang (2017, JNeurosci).\nKey innovation: The ratio of long-range excitation (LRE) to feedforward inhibition (FFI) controls functional connectivity between brain regions. This E/I balance tuning enables fitting personalized brain network models to empirical functional connectivity and explains individual differences in cognitive performance (speed-accuracy trade-off in intelligence tests).\n" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/experiments/Schirner2023_MultiscaleBNM_DM> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Multiscale BNM: Decision-Making with E/I Balance Tuning" .
